misc.lust:1:1  stop only works inside a loop.
misc.lust:2:1  skip only works inside a loop.
misc.lust:4:13  one comparison at a time. Join them with &&: is a < b && b < c?
misc.lust:5:11  < compares numbers, but this has a string.
misc.lust:6:16  random's lowest number comes first: random(1, 6)
misc.lust:7:16  random takes whole numbers, but this is a float.
misc.lust:8:1  print takes one thing to show: print(x)
misc.lust:9:1  random(…) gives back an int, but nothing uses it. Put it in a variable: int x = random(…);
misc.lust:10:14  either needs a yes-or-no answer, but this is an int. Compare it with something, like either hp 0? … or …
misc.lust:11:25  both sides of either must be the same type, but one is an int and the other is a string.
misc.lust:12:6  wait takes a number of seconds, but this is a string.
misc.lust:13:6  can't wait a negative number of seconds.
